BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wellness Collective Moab": "https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wellness_collective
URL:https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar
SUMMARY:Monthly Ayurveda Talk- What’s my Dosha
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260828T190000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260828T200000
UID:dd3b24e4df17c92456c38397ad17d7dd@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Kathy for an introduction to the Ayurvedic doshas and dis
 cover why understanding your unique constitution can be a helpful guide to
  health and well-being. Rooted in a holistic system practiced for thousand
 s of years\, Ayurveda recognizes that each person has a unique balance of 
 physical\, mental\, and emotional qualities that influence how we experien
 ce the world. In this workshop\, we’ll explore the three doshas—Vata\,
  Pitta\, and Kapha—and discuss how they shape our tendencies\, strengths
 \, and common patterns of imbalance. We’ll also talk about why identifyi
 ng your dosha can be a valuable starting point for supporting wellness\, w
 hile recognizing that it doesn’t tell the whole story. This workshop is 
 intended to be educational\, reflective\, and approachable for anyone curi
 ous about learning more about Ayurveda and how its principles can be appli
 ed to everyday life. No prior experience with Ayurveda is needed. By Donat
 ion – Suggested $15–25
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532\, USA
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wellness Collective Moab": "https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wellness_collective
URL:https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar
SUMMARY:Qi-Gong with Cody
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260829T080000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260829T090000
UID:8211ef71073f38e8b8841f7bc20d56fd@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Zhineng Qigong is a powerful mind-body practice rooted in anci
 ent Chinese healing traditions and adapted for modern times. This gentle y
 et profound system blends slow movement\, sound\, visualization\, and medi
 tation to help individuals cultivate inner peace\, restore balance\, and e
 nhance vitality. By consciously connecting with the energy of life—what 
 some may call qi or universal life force—participants are invited into a
  process of holistic healing: physically\, emotionally\, and spiritually. 
 One of the most accessible forms of Qigong\, Zhineng emphasizes connection
  over complexity. Its principles can be embraced by people of all ages\, b
 ackgrounds\, and physical abilities. Cody teaches from a place of lived ex
 perience\, having found this practice deeply healing and transformative in
  his own journey. His classes focus on cultivating shared energy through g
 roup practice\, empowering individuals to tap into their innate wisdom and
  live with greater purpose and presence.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
